[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="DialogueData" format=3 uid="uid://6pkoadhx1qxg"]

[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://dd85gxidfhqxl" path="res://systems/dialogue/dialogue_data.gd" id="1_dlg"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_dlg")
source = "# Examiner Sudo: rank examiner. Dry, patient.
# Exams are quests (exam_operator, exam_architect, exam_engineer, exam_defragmenter). Passing reports 'rank_up' for the rank system.
# Every exam is sat in the sandbox (> exam <rank>); the Defragmenter exam lends sorting.
# The Operator and Architect exams are sat in the sandbox (> exam operator, > exam architect, see
# ExamChamber), and can be retaken for a better grade once passed.
~ start
# A Yard Sweep deleted Sudo's exam archive (YardCrates CargoB): said once
@ crate_news:CargoB -> loss_archive
@ quest_active:q06c_root_access -> coming_along
@ quest_ready:guild_expedition -> ready_guild
@ quest_ready:exam_defragmenter -> pass_defragmenter
@ quest_ready:time_slice -> ready_slice
@ quest_ready:exam_engineer -> pass_engineer
@ quest_ready:exam_operator -> pass_operator
@ quest_ready:exam_architect -> pass_architect
@ quest_ready:exam_strategist -> pass_strategist
# A save that passed the old Defragmenter checklist holds the rank with no grade: the exam was rewritten
@ exam_ungraded:defragmenter -> rewritten_defragmenter
@ quest_active:exam_defragmenter -> ready_defragmenter
@ quest_active:exam_engineer -> ready_engineer
@ quest_active:exam_operator -> ready_operator
@ quest_active:exam_architect -> ready_architect
@ quest_active:exam_strategist -> ready_strategist
@ can_start:exam_defragmenter -> offer_defragmenter
@ can_start:time_slice -> offer_slice
@ quest_active:time_slice -> remind_slice
@ can_start:exam_engineer -> offer_engineer
@ can_start:exam_operator -> offer_operator
@ can_start:exam_architect -> offer_architect
@ can_start:exam_strategist -> offer_strategist
@ can_start:guild_expedition -> offer_guild
@ quest_active:guild_expedition -> remind_guild
@ quest_done:exam_defragmenter -> retake_defragmenter
@ quest_done:exam_engineer -> retake_engineer
@ quest_done:exam_strategist -> retake_strategist
@ quest_done:exam_architect -> retake_architect
@ quest_done:exam_operator -> retake_operator
-> idle

~ coming_along
Sudo: Hex is going through that gate. So am I.
Sudo: Exams don't grade themselves. Unfortunately.
* OTHER EXAMS -> retake_strategist
* GOODBYE -> end

~ offer_operator
Sudo: Show me your script. I grade logic, not luck.
# NEW line below: ties the exam to the Gate Guard fight
Sudo: The Gate Guard swings slow. A wasteful script won't wait for your opening. A patient one will.
* ACCEPT -> accept_operator
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_operator
> start_quest exam_operator
# NEW lines below: the sandbox exam
Sudo: The exam runs in my sandbox. Test processes, closing in from every side.
Sudo: Your skill reacts when they crowd you, or it doesn't. Read the spec, then run it.
-> ready_operator

~ ready_operator
Sudo: The sandbox is ready when you are.
* ENTER THE SANDBOX -> go_operator
* NOT YET -> end

~ go_operator
> exam operator

~ retake_operator
Sudo: Efficiency is just laziness with a plan.
* RETAKE THE OPERATOR EXAM -> go_operator
* LEAVE -> end

~ offer_strategist
Sudo: Your scripts only know what's true right now. This whole place is what happens when memory goes wrong.
Sudo: The Strategist exam. The Registrar let me replay Checkpoint's quarantine logs into a sealed bay.
Sudo: Three samples from out there, and one new tool: a script that remembers.
* ACCEPT -> accept_strategist
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_strategist
> start_quest exam_strategist
Sudo: I'll lend you a registry. A list of every process you've touched, like the Registrar's books. Add to it with one rule, check it with another. A dead process drops off it, and the whole thing clears when the fight ends. In the middle of one, though, a list nobody reads is just a leak.
-> ready_strategist

~ ready_strategist
Sudo: The bay is sealed and the samples are loaded. Ready when you are.
* ENTER THE SANDBOX -> go_strategist
* NOT YET -> end

~ go_strategist
> exam strategist

~ pass_strategist
> turn_in exam_strategist
> report rank_up strategist
Sudo: It remembered, and it let go. Rank up. Strategist.
Sudo: The registry is yours now, and so is set C. A plan is just a loop you haven't run yet.
-> end

~ retake_strategist
Sudo: A plan is just a loop you haven't run yet.
* RETAKE THE STRATEGIST EXAM -> go_strategist
* LEAVE -> end

~ offer_architect
Sudo: Past the Gate, scripts get longer. Long scripts that never stop get you killed.
Sudo: The Architect exam. A loop that knows when to quit.
* ACCEPT -> accept_architect
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_architect
> start_quest exam_architect
Sudo: I'll lend you loops in the sandbox, and if blocks. A while, or a for with an if that breaks. Your choice.
Sudo: Repeat while it's worth it. Stop when it isn't. Read the spec, then run it.
-> ready_architect

~ ready_architect
Sudo: The sandbox is ready when you are.
* ENTER THE SANDBOX -> go_architect
* NOT YET -> end

~ go_architect
> exam architect

~ retake_architect
Sudo: Structure is just patience written down.
* RETAKE THE ARCHITECT EXAM -> go_architect
* RETAKE THE OPERATOR EXAM -> go_operator
* LEAVE -> end

~ offer_guild
Sudo: The Compiler Guild sent an expedition into the Null, years before your convoy. My examiner went with them.
Sudo: She graded everything. Campsites. Weather. Me. The last log came from a place the Guild called the Expedition's End.
Sudo: Find out what happened. Bring me their logs.
* ACCEPT -> accept_guild
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_guild
> start_quest guild_expedition
Sudo: South-west of here. If she's still there, she'll want to see your work. Bring a lean script.
-> end

~ remind_guild
Sudo: Three logs, and whatever is left of her. South-west portal.
-> end

~ ready_guild
Sudo: You found her.
> turn_in guild_expedition
Sudo: She called the Null the best-written code she'd ever audited. She wasn't wrong. That was the problem.
Sudo: Thank you. I'll grade the rest of your exams a little more kindly. No, I won't.
-> end

~ offer_defragmenter
Sudo: The last exam. After this there's nothing left for me to grade.
Sudo: Past here is the Stack Trace. Everything the Core remembers, in pieces, and the pieces only take a hit in the right order.
Sudo: The memory isn't lost. It's out of order. A Defragmenter puts it back. I don't let anyone in there who can't.
* ACCEPT -> accept_defragmenter
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_defragmenter
> start_quest exam_defragmenter
Sudo: I'll lend you sorting. Your registry has always kept enemies in the order they joined. Now you choose the order.
Sudo: registry.sort, key equals hp: least life first. Then registry, zero, is the one at the front. Read that, and hit it hardest.
Sudo: The samples are fragmented. Out of order they barely feel you. Kill one out of order and the rest knit back together.
Sudo: Fifteen fragments. Put twelve back in order and I'll call it defragmented.
Sudo: Pass it and the Stack Trace is yours to walk.
-> ready_defragmenter

~ ready_defragmenter
Sudo: The sandbox is loaded. Sort it, then take it from the front.
* ENTER THE SANDBOX -> go_defragmenter
* NOT YET -> end

~ go_defragmenter
> exam defragmenter

~ rewritten_defragmenter
Sudo: Your Defragmenter rank. I wrote it on you for a checklist. A loop, the registry, two conditions.
Sudo: I've rewritten the exam since. The Core's memory comes back in pieces, and pieces only fit in order. That's what a Defragmenter is for.
Sudo: Sorting is already yours. The sandbox has fifteen fragments in it. Put twelve back in order and I'll give the rank a grade. A grade is worth script points.
* ENTER THE SANDBOX -> go_defragmenter
* OTHER EXAMS -> retake_defragmenter
* NOT NOW -> end

~ retake_defragmenter
Sudo: Order is just memory with a plan.
* RETAKE THE DEFRAGMENTER EXAM -> go_defragmenter
* RETAKE THE ENGINEER EXAM -> go_engineer
* LEAVE -> end

~ pass_defragmenter
> turn_in exam_defragmenter
> report rank_up defragmenter
Sudo: Every piece, in order, and nothing knit back. Defragmenter. I've never written that rank on anyone.
Sudo: Sorting is yours now. The Stack Trace is open: every pack in there is in pieces. The Root Process calls its adds in pieces too.
Sudo: Whatever you decide at the bottom of all this, decide it efficiently.
-> end

~ offer_engineer
Sudo: You've seen what it does. The Mimic. The husks. A convoy deleted in one book and inbound in another. The Null copies.
Sudo: Past The Threshold it copies you. Your skills, your scripts. Copies drift: change yours and theirs don't know.
Sudo: The Engineer exam, before I let you out there. Don't copy. Reference.
* ACCEPT -> accept_engineer
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_engineer
> start_quest exam_engineer
Sudo: I'll lend you routines. Write the lines once, in routines.gd. Give them a name.
Sudo: Then any skill can run them with one line: call, and the name. One block, however much the routine does. Change the routine, and every skill that calls it changes with it.
Sudo: Three skills, one routine. The samples are copies of your own fights, so they'll know your habits.
-> ready_engineer

~ ready_engineer
Sudo: The sandbox is loaded. Three skills, one routine.
* ENTER THE SANDBOX -> go_engineer
* NOT YET -> end

~ go_engineer
> exam engineer

~ retake_engineer
Sudo: The Null copies. An Engineer references.
* RETAKE THE ENGINEER EXAM -> go_engineer
* RETAKE THE STRATEGIST EXAM -> go_strategist
* LEAVE -> end

~ fail
Sudo: Too many wasted steps. Trim it and try again.

~ pass_operator
> turn_in exam_operator
> report rank_up operator
Sudo: Clean and efficient. Rank up. Operator.
Sudo: Retake it whenever you like. I keep your best grade.
-> end

~ pass_architect
> turn_in exam_architect
> report rank_up architect
Sudo: It stopped when it should. Rank up. Architect.
Sudo: Loops are yours now, outside the sandbox too. Retake it whenever you like.
-> end

~ pass_engineer
> turn_in exam_engineer
> report rank_up engineer
Sudo: One source, three skills, and none of them drifted. Rank up. Engineer.
Sudo: Routines are yours now. Write a thing once, and let everything else point at it. The Fray is open.
Sudo: One more thing. When the Null copies a script with a call in it, it copies the call. Not the routine. Think about who else is pointing at your routines.gd.
-> end

~ loss_archive
> report crate_mourned CargoB
Sudo: My archive went into C-0's queue. Every grade I ever wrote. Every examiner before me.
Sudo: I remember most of them. That's the trouble with remembering. Most.
Sudo: If you're in the Sweep anyway, it'll be in a cage with my name on it. I'd grade you kindly. I'd try.
-> start

~ offer_slice
Sudo: The last floor before the Kernel. The Scheduler. The Null decides what runs next in there, and you can't go round it.
Sudo: It writes into your kernel.gd while you stand in it. A new line every forty-five seconds. It's the only exam the Null ever set, and it doesn't grade on a curve.
* ACCEPT -> accept_slice
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_slice
> start_quest time_slice
Sudo: Clear it. Write your kernel for all four of its lines, not the one you're looking at.
-> end

~ remind_slice
Sudo: The Scheduler. Every forty-five seconds, a new line that isn't yours. Plan for all of them.
-> end

~ ready_slice
> turn_in time_slice
Sudo: You passed an exam I didn't write. I'm not sure how I feel about that. I'll record it anyway.
-> start

~ idle
@ crate_restored:CargoB -> idle_archive
Sudo: Efficiency is just laziness with a plan.
-> end

~ idle_archive
Sudo: My archive's back on the yard floor. I checked every grade. You're in it now."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://dd85gxidfhqxl"
